WEBVTT

00:00:12.514 --> 00:00:15.014
Narumi residence...

00:00:15.014 --> 00:00:16.814
Oh, it's you, brother...

00:00:17.824 --> 00:00:21.994
I'm going to pursue the
mystery of the Blade Children.

00:00:21.994 --> 00:00:24.824
Until I attain the unseen
truth with these two hands...

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:26.984
Tell Madoka for me too.

00:00:31.004 --> 00:00:32.594
Huh?

00:00:45.314 --> 00:00:46.944
<i>I had a dream about that day.</i>

00:00:47.314 --> 00:00:52.824
<i>Everyone is searching for a new world</i>

00:00:52.824 --> 00:00:58.924
<i>to attain that overflowing dream.</i>

00:00:58.924 --> 00:01:04.434
<i>They all jump over the horizon,</i>

00:01:04.434 --> 00:01:13.204
<i>regardless of what lies beyond.</i>

00:01:16.044 --> 00:01:20.954
<i>We've run,</i>

00:01:20.954 --> 00:01:23.424
<i>we've dived into hope,</i>

00:01:23.424 --> 00:01:26.294
<i>and forgotten only courage.</i>

00:01:26.294 --> 00:01:31.024
<i>And we've been swept away by the crowd</i>

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:35.694
<i>only to lose something dear to us.</i>

00:01:39.004 --> 00:01:41.374
<i>I smile with a twisted face,</i>

00:01:41.374 --> 00:01:46.974
<i>and it was the best smile I could put on.</i>

00:01:46.974 --> 00:01:48.104
<i>And it was the best smile I could put on.</i>

00:01:49.374 --> 00:01:51.484
<i>The inside of my mask overflowed with tears</i>

00:01:51.484 --> 00:01:59.124
<i>so I covered my wet mask
with yet another mask.</i>

00:01:59.124 --> 00:02:03.964
<i>I continue to walk through
the flat battleground,</i>

00:02:03.964 --> 00:02:09.194
<i>and I struggle, unable to warp.</i>

00:02:09.194 --> 00:02:19.304
<i>The dream waits quietly on a cape far away.</i>

00:02:19.304 --> 00:02:24.044
<i>Even if I fumble around clumsily,</i>

00:02:24.044 --> 00:02:28.784
<i>I'm sure I'll still be
able to make it there.</i>

00:02:35.854 --> 00:02:37.944
Oh, crap. I slept too long.

00:02:42.094 --> 00:02:45.664
<i>Come to think of it,
it was on this very day...</i>

00:02:45.664 --> 00:02:48.994
<i>On this day two years ago,
my older brother disappeared.</i>

00:02:50.534 --> 00:02:53.734
<i>"I'm going to pursue the
mystery of the Blade Children..."</i>

00:02:53.734 --> 00:02:57.604
<i>And with those words,
he vanished without a trace...</i>

00:03:07.014 --> 00:03:08.724
Are you alright?!

00:03:08.724 --> 00:03:10.274
Say something!

00:03:12.224 --> 00:03:13.594
What's going on?

00:03:13.594 --> 00:03:16.894
Talk about dangerous, there's no fence here!

00:03:16.894 --> 00:03:20.024
Did you do this? Did you push her off?!

00:03:23.464 --> 00:03:24.454
Huh?

00:03:25.934 --> 00:03:30.274
"The Spiral of Destiny"

00:03:42.684 --> 00:03:44.844
Thank you for coming, Assistant Inspector!

00:03:44.844 --> 00:03:45.954
Give me the details.

00:03:45.954 --> 00:03:46.754
Yes, ma'am.

00:03:46.754 --> 00:03:49.224
The injured girl is a 2nd-year
student at Tsukiomi Academy,

00:03:49.224 --> 00:03:51.024
Sayoko Shiranagatani.

00:03:51.024 --> 00:03:53.094
She fell from a landing on the 5th floor.

00:03:53.094 --> 00:03:55.964
Miraculously, the truck parked
directly below acted as a cushion

00:03:55.964 --> 00:03:58.494
so she only received light injuries.

00:03:58.494 --> 00:04:01.794
But she's in shock, so she's
unable to respond to any questions.

00:04:01.794 --> 00:04:04.864
A fence from the landing was
found lying at the scene.

00:04:04.864 --> 00:04:08.004
An accident, suicide,
or an attempted murder?

00:04:08.004 --> 00:04:09.874
They're all possibilities here.

00:04:09.874 --> 00:04:13.314
Given the situation, it's highly
unlikely this was a suicide attempt.

00:04:13.314 --> 00:04:14.714
How's that?

00:04:14.714 --> 00:04:17.984
Don't you think there's anything
strange about those glasses?

00:04:17.984 --> 00:04:22.254
Well, they are pretty lame for
high school girls these days!

00:04:22.254 --> 00:04:24.024
That's not what I mean.

00:04:24.024 --> 00:04:26.794
People who commit suicide generally
worry about their appearance

00:04:26.794 --> 00:04:27.794
before they die.

00:04:27.794 --> 00:04:29.664
Do you think a girl her age

00:04:29.664 --> 00:04:32.324
would kill herself while wearing those?

00:04:32.324 --> 00:04:36.934
But perhaps she was fond of the
way she looked with glasses on...

00:04:36.934 --> 00:04:40.174
Did you even look at her school ID?

00:04:40.174 --> 00:04:43.004
She doesn't normally wear glasses.

00:04:43.004 --> 00:04:46.614
So she wouldn't wear them
if she didn't have to...

00:04:46.614 --> 00:04:47.844
You're right...

00:04:47.844 --> 00:04:51.614
If you're going to call yourself a
detective, learn how to use your brain.

00:04:51.614 --> 00:04:52.514
Yes, ma'am.

00:04:52.514 --> 00:04:59.224
<i>Hey! So you think 1st-year student
Narumi-san did it, Sonobe-sensei?!</i>

00:04:59.224 --> 00:05:02.424
I don't want to point any
fingers at you, either,

00:05:02.424 --> 00:05:07.964
but I did see you on the landing
immediately after she fell...

00:05:07.964 --> 00:05:10.034
Oh my! Eyewitness testimony!

00:05:10.034 --> 00:05:12.104
<i>What now, Narumi-san?!</i>

00:05:12.104 --> 00:05:14.574
I already told you I didn't do it.

00:05:14.574 --> 00:05:17.644
Besides, nobody's so dumb that
they'd try to kill someone

00:05:17.644 --> 00:05:19.974
by pushing them onto a truck.

00:05:19.974 --> 00:05:24.014
But that truck just
happened to be there today;

00:05:24.014 --> 00:05:26.684
it's not the car that's
usually parked there.

00:05:26.684 --> 00:05:31.124
<i>How do you explain this, Narumi-san?</i>

00:05:31.124 --> 00:05:34.094
I'm telling you, I didn't do it.

00:05:37.924 --> 00:05:40.164
Is something the matter?

00:05:40.164 --> 00:05:41.194
No...

00:05:41.194 --> 00:05:42.864
Who are you, anyway?

00:05:42.864 --> 00:05:44.104
Oh, sorry about that!

00:05:44.104 --> 00:05:45.504
I'm a 2nd-year student at Tsukiomi Academy

00:05:45.504 --> 00:05:46.604
and head of the school newspaper!

00:05:46.604 --> 00:05:48.504
My name is Hiyono Yuizaki!

00:05:48.504 --> 00:05:49.974
I'm pleased to make your acquaintance!

00:05:49.974 --> 00:05:50.644
Alright, alright.

00:05:50.644 --> 00:05:53.014
Sorry to interrupt your little fun,

00:05:53.014 --> 00:05:55.944
but it's the police's
job to question people.

00:06:00.414 --> 00:06:03.424
<i>According to Sonobe-sensei,
who was an eyewitness...</i>

00:06:03.424 --> 00:06:08.954
"Actually, I transferred to this
school only a few days ago,

00:06:08.954 --> 00:06:12.764
so I used my lunch break to
take a walk around the campus.

00:06:12.764 --> 00:06:16.234
All of a sudden, I heard a girl scream.

00:06:16.234 --> 00:06:21.174
Immediately afterward, she and
the fence fell from the landing.

00:06:21.174 --> 00:06:23.104
Without thinking, I rushed over to her.

00:06:23.104 --> 00:06:27.774
Just then, I noticed him
looking at me from the landing."

00:06:27.774 --> 00:06:32.344
That's what he told us.

00:06:32.344 --> 00:06:35.824
What exactly were you doing up there?

00:06:35.824 --> 00:06:38.054
I was taking a nap on the roof.

00:06:38.054 --> 00:06:40.624
I heard a scream when I
started to go back down,

00:06:40.624 --> 00:06:43.394
so I checked to see what it was.

00:06:43.394 --> 00:06:45.524
You got a problem with that?

00:06:45.524 --> 00:06:47.634
Assistant Inspector!
He obviously did it!

00:06:47.634 --> 00:06:49.504
That's enough...

00:06:49.504 --> 00:06:54.274
To continue, did you notice anybody
else when you were on the landing?

00:06:54.274 --> 00:06:57.274
Nope. It was just me.

00:06:57.274 --> 00:06:59.074
Talk about stupid!

00:06:59.074 --> 00:07:00.514
By saying that, you've just admitted

00:07:00.514 --> 00:07:04.414
that you're the only person in the
world who could have pushed her off!

00:07:04.414 --> 00:07:06.654
Which means you did it!

00:07:06.654 --> 00:07:10.424
Sorry, but I don't have time for this.

00:07:10.424 --> 00:07:12.524
I'll be in trouble if
I don't get home soon.

00:07:12.524 --> 00:07:14.754
Is your mommy going to yell at you?

00:07:14.754 --> 00:07:15.654
No...

00:07:15.654 --> 00:07:18.524
His beautiful sister is
going to yell at him

00:07:18.524 --> 00:07:22.334
if he doesn't hurry home
and get dinner ready.

00:07:22.334 --> 00:07:25.004
Your perceptive abilities
are lacking, Wataya!

00:07:25.004 --> 00:07:26.904
What's my full name?

00:07:26.904 --> 00:07:28.674
Assistant Inspector Madoka Narumi.

00:07:28.674 --> 00:07:31.104
And his full name?

00:07:31.104 --> 00:07:33.474
Ayumu Narumi...

00:07:33.474 --> 00:07:35.274
Narumi? Huh?

00:07:35.274 --> 00:07:37.714
There's no "huh" about it...

00:07:37.714 --> 00:07:39.354
So he's your...

00:07:39.354 --> 00:07:41.784
He's my brother-in-law.

00:07:42.754 --> 00:07:48.594
I'll let you go for now, but I hope
you realize the situation you're in.

00:07:48.594 --> 00:07:51.614
Man, I sure got myself into a real mess...

00:07:54.594 --> 00:07:59.064
<i>So that detective is actually
Narumi-san's older sister!</i>

00:07:59.064 --> 00:08:02.594
Things looks like they're
about to get interesting!

00:08:03.844 --> 00:08:05.644
What is this?!

00:08:05.644 --> 00:08:08.344
Just what it looks like - curry.

00:08:08.344 --> 00:08:13.084
Yes...This is definitely
nothing other than curry, but...

00:08:13.084 --> 00:08:13.784
...that's not what I meant!

00:08:13.784 --> 00:08:16.124
You said you were going to make
Mediterranean-style bouillabaisse

00:08:16.124 --> 00:08:18.324
And mountain risotto!

00:08:18.324 --> 00:08:20.424
Where's the sophisticated
fragrance of saffron?!

00:08:20.424 --> 00:08:22.864
Where's the texture of the bracken?!

00:08:22.864 --> 00:08:27.664
I was busy this whole afternoon being
treated like a ruthless criminal!

00:08:27.664 --> 00:08:30.434
As if I could cook
anything fancy that quick!

00:08:30.434 --> 00:08:32.104
And what is this?!

00:08:32.104 --> 00:08:35.304
I thought it was strange you
didn't use a pot to make the curry...

00:08:35.304 --> 00:08:37.044
But I found it!

00:08:37.044 --> 00:08:39.644
The most incriminating piece of
evidence: A bag of pre-made curry!

00:08:39.644 --> 00:08:41.974
Wow, you're a great detective.

00:08:41.974 --> 00:08:43.974
Are you mocking me?!

00:08:55.724 --> 00:09:02.964
<i>It's been two years to the day
when Kiyotaka-san disappeared...</i>

00:09:02.964 --> 00:09:07.134
Say, you act pretty stuck-up at work, huh?

00:09:07.134 --> 00:09:08.634
What're you talking about?

00:09:08.634 --> 00:09:12.344
I'm not stuck-up or
unsociable in the least.

00:09:12.344 --> 00:09:16.414
You can't deny that you're selfish
and treat people like crap, though.

00:09:16.414 --> 00:09:17.544
Ow.

00:09:17.544 --> 00:09:19.854
What was that for? It's the truth.

00:09:19.854 --> 00:09:22.684
Things are seriously looking
bad for you, you know.

00:09:22.684 --> 00:09:23.954
As things stand now,

00:09:23.954 --> 00:09:28.524
there was nobody else there
who could've pushed her off.

00:09:28.524 --> 00:09:31.294
Nope. It was just me.

00:09:31.294 --> 00:09:34.034
Your testimony was the clincher.

00:09:34.034 --> 00:09:36.064
It's highly unlikely
that it was a suicide,

00:09:36.064 --> 00:09:39.934
and it looks more like a case of
someone forcefully pushing her off

00:09:39.934 --> 00:09:41.834
than it does a simple accident.

00:09:41.834 --> 00:09:46.374
And as things stand now, you were
the only one who could've done that.

00:09:46.374 --> 00:09:48.944
In other words, unless
someone used a special trick

00:09:48.944 --> 00:09:51.144
I'm the only one who could've done it.

00:09:51.144 --> 00:09:53.484
A special trick?

00:09:53.484 --> 00:09:56.324
Figuring out that trick
comes first and foremost.

00:09:56.324 --> 00:09:59.184
What exactly is this trick
you're talking about?

00:09:59.184 --> 00:10:01.754
I dunno, I'm just an amateur.

00:10:01.754 --> 00:10:04.194
Guess I'll wash some dishes now.

00:10:04.194 --> 00:10:07.734
You've figured out something, haven't you?

00:10:07.734 --> 00:10:11.734
That reminds me, Sonobe
needs to be watched.

00:10:11.734 --> 00:10:17.174
Remember how he talked like he
was an expert on that parking lot,

00:10:17.174 --> 00:10:18.744
even though he just got a job there?

00:10:18.744 --> 00:10:19.644
Yeah...

00:10:19.644 --> 00:10:22.314
Not a single teacher would
have known that sort of thing

00:10:22.314 --> 00:10:24.984
without having checked out
the school beforehand.

00:10:24.984 --> 00:10:27.884
In other words, he really did his homework

00:10:27.884 --> 00:10:29.654
on the area around that landing.

00:10:29.654 --> 00:10:33.594
But he rushed straight up
to her when it happened.

00:10:33.594 --> 00:10:37.064
He was on the ground, so if he
did push her off the landing,

00:10:37.064 --> 00:10:40.834
he would need one heck of a
long arm to reach up that far.

00:10:40.834 --> 00:10:44.234
That's what I'm saying, unless
someone used a special trick,

00:10:44.234 --> 00:10:46.164
I'm the only one who could've done it.

00:10:47.434 --> 00:10:52.744
<i>Plus Sonobe purposely shouted
at me after it happened!</i>

00:10:52.744 --> 00:10:56.484
Did you do this? Did you push her off?!

00:10:56.484 --> 00:10:59.854
<i>Everyone focused their
attention on me when he shouted,</i>

00:10:59.854 --> 00:11:01.714
<i>and during that brief moment
he picked something up</i>

00:11:01.714 --> 00:11:04.484
<i>and stuffed it in his pocket...</i>

00:11:04.484 --> 00:11:05.324
Ayumu...

00:11:05.324 --> 00:11:07.394
Hey, Ayumu!

00:11:07.394 --> 00:11:10.164
Why're you so quiet all of a sudden?

00:11:10.164 --> 00:11:13.064
If you don't explain everything then
you'll never be cleared of suspicion!

00:11:13.064 --> 00:11:15.194
It doesn't really matter to me.

00:11:15.194 --> 00:11:17.604
What?! This entire thing concerns you!

00:11:17.604 --> 00:11:20.474
I'm just an ordinary 1st-year
high school student,

00:11:20.474 --> 00:11:23.594
so I'll leave all the detective
work to you, Detective.

00:11:26.614 --> 00:11:30.744
You always act indifferent to everything...

00:11:39.354 --> 00:11:41.954
<i>Indifferent to everything...</i>

00:11:41.954 --> 00:11:43.894
<i>Definitely.</i>

00:11:44.794 --> 00:11:49.034
<i>I've locked myself up inside myself.</i>

00:11:49.034 --> 00:11:50.934
<i>Am I scared of getting
involved in something</i>

00:11:50.934 --> 00:11:53.134
<i>and having a knock on the door?</i>

00:11:53.134 --> 00:11:58.334
<i>Or maybe I'm scared of being
dragged into the darkness.</i>

00:11:59.444 --> 00:12:02.574
"Until I attain the unseen
truth with these two hands..."

00:12:06.044 --> 00:12:08.274
<i>I'm not like my brother...</i>

00:12:24.964 --> 00:12:28.304
<i>How are you feeling, Sayoko-sama?</i>

00:12:32.844 --> 00:12:34.474
<i>Sayoko-sama...</i>

00:12:36.484 --> 00:12:41.214
I had no idea the victim has had
amnesia for such a long time...

00:12:41.214 --> 00:12:42.484
I'll feel so bad for her

00:12:42.484 --> 00:12:45.954
if things get even worse
for her after this incident...

00:12:45.954 --> 00:12:49.354
At any rate, that note is
the key to solving this case.

00:12:49.354 --> 00:12:51.624
"Go to the 5th floor landing."
Yeah, that note we found in her desk...

00:12:51.624 --> 00:12:54.064
"There you can meet someone
who knows about your past."
Yeah, that note we found in her desk...

00:12:54.064 --> 00:12:58.534
"There you can meet someone
who knows about your past."
There's no question that someone
lured her to the landing...

00:12:58.534 --> 00:13:01.434
What do you suppose the
secret behind her past is?

00:13:01.434 --> 00:13:05.144
The reason she went to the landing
was so she could find out too.

00:13:05.144 --> 00:13:08.514
She still can't respond
to anyone's questions,

00:13:08.514 --> 00:13:11.604
and her family is on guard
for some strange reason.

00:13:18.384 --> 00:13:22.154
<i>There was nothing my brother couldn't do.</i>

00:13:23.594 --> 00:13:26.564
<i>I wanted to be just like him.</i>

00:13:26.564 --> 00:13:29.254
<i>But it was a dream never meant to be.</i>

00:13:31.564 --> 00:13:34.934
<i>He had become a world-renowned
pianist in his teens,</i>

00:13:34.934 --> 00:13:38.074
<i>but then he quit like it was nothing...</i>

00:13:38.074 --> 00:13:42.774
<i>In his twenties, he was referred to by
the police force as the Divine Brain...</i>

00:13:45.214 --> 00:13:47.554
<i>At some point, I may have
started to detest him</i>

00:13:47.554 --> 00:13:51.954
<i>as I tried to follow in his footsteps.</i>

00:13:53.154 --> 00:13:55.354
Found you, Mr. Criminal!

00:13:55.354 --> 00:13:58.624
Who're you calling Mr. Criminal?
What do you want?

00:13:58.624 --> 00:14:02.334
I just wondered if you
had heard the rumor!

00:14:02.334 --> 00:14:03.104
Rumor?

00:14:03.104 --> 00:14:04.664
To be more precise...

00:14:04.664 --> 00:14:09.104
I was hoping you could tell me what
it felt like when you pushed her off!

00:14:09.104 --> 00:14:11.444
I already told you, I didn't do it.

00:14:11.444 --> 00:14:14.674
But everyone's whispering
that the one responsible

00:14:14.674 --> 00:14:16.814
was 1st-year student Ayumu Narumi.

00:14:16.814 --> 00:14:18.884
How did the rumor spread so fast?

00:14:18.884 --> 00:14:23.884
Maybe because there's someone
aggressively spreading it around?

00:14:23.884 --> 00:14:25.124
Sonobe?

00:14:25.124 --> 00:14:27.524
Hey, that's him! He's the guy...

00:14:27.524 --> 00:14:30.124
Yikes! Talk about scary...

00:14:30.124 --> 00:14:32.224
You're famous all of a sudden!

00:14:32.224 --> 00:14:35.164
I hear he's the one who did it!

00:14:35.164 --> 00:14:37.404
But supposedly there's still no proof.

00:14:37.404 --> 00:14:40.404
What will you do now, Mr. Criminal?

00:14:40.404 --> 00:14:41.834
Nothing really.

00:14:41.834 --> 00:14:45.644
So you plan to remain the object
of attention like this then?

00:14:45.644 --> 00:14:47.114
I don't really mind it.

00:14:47.114 --> 00:14:51.644
I didn't think you were the
kind who loves attention...

00:14:51.644 --> 00:14:55.854
What annoys me the most is when
people follow me around everywhere.

00:14:55.854 --> 00:14:57.324
So just leave me alone.

00:14:57.324 --> 00:14:58.184
No!

00:14:58.184 --> 00:14:59.224
No?

00:14:59.224 --> 00:15:01.894
This is hardly enough information
to make a newspaper article!

00:15:01.894 --> 00:15:05.424
If I'm annoying you, then let's find
who really did it, Mr. Criminal!

00:15:05.424 --> 00:15:08.334
I'll even help you! What do you say?!

00:15:11.504 --> 00:15:14.194
"Faculty Office"

00:15:14.774 --> 00:15:18.574
You want me to look like a
bad guy no matter what.

00:15:18.574 --> 00:15:21.674
I just told it like I saw it.

00:15:21.674 --> 00:15:25.544
Then I'll tell it like I saw it.

00:15:25.544 --> 00:15:28.314
I'm going to figure out your trick!

00:15:30.684 --> 00:15:33.054
Talk about scary!

00:15:33.054 --> 00:15:38.164
<i>It's amazing that Shiranagatani-san
survived a fall from this height!</i>

00:15:38.164 --> 00:15:39.194
Yeah.

00:15:39.194 --> 00:15:41.794
Now that I think about it, I hear
she was wearing glasses at the time,

00:15:41.794 --> 00:15:43.504
which is pretty rare for her.

00:15:43.504 --> 00:15:44.604
Rare?

00:15:44.604 --> 00:15:49.074
According to "Hiyono's Data", she
almost never wears her glasses

00:15:49.074 --> 00:15:50.674
except during class.

00:15:50.674 --> 00:15:53.074
What the heck is "Hiyono's Data"?

00:15:53.074 --> 00:15:56.484
My personal notebook filled with
information about the school!

00:15:56.484 --> 00:16:00.954
It's how I make a living, so I'll
never ever show it to anyone else!

00:16:00.954 --> 00:16:02.484
I don't wanna see it.

00:16:02.484 --> 00:16:05.884
<i>She must have put her glasses on</i>

00:16:05.884 --> 00:16:08.954
<i>because she was trying to
see something from up here.</i>

00:16:08.954 --> 00:16:10.794
<i>But what?</i>

00:16:10.794 --> 00:16:13.094
Hey, Hiyono!

00:16:13.094 --> 00:16:15.094
We're going to lunch!

00:16:15.094 --> 00:16:17.534
Okay! I'll catch up in a little bit!

00:16:17.534 --> 00:16:19.054
That's scary!

00:16:23.304 --> 00:16:25.244
That's it!

00:16:26.004 --> 00:16:26.814
Huh?

00:16:26.814 --> 00:16:29.934
The truth has been played.

00:16:32.314 --> 00:16:34.584
It's from Ayumu.

00:16:34.584 --> 00:16:36.254
Hi, what's up?

00:16:36.254 --> 00:16:38.724
There's something I
want you to check into.

00:16:38.724 --> 00:16:40.194
Okay...

00:16:40.194 --> 00:16:43.624
So that has to do with
the real culprit then?

00:16:43.624 --> 00:16:45.954
Got it. I'll look into it right away.

00:16:47.994 --> 00:16:51.094
<i>He's Kiyotaka-san's little
brother, all right...</i>

00:16:58.644 --> 00:17:01.214
<i>Sonobe-sensei...</i>

00:17:01.214 --> 00:17:02.774
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:17:02.774 --> 00:17:06.014
That's alright. What did you
need to talk to me about?

00:17:06.014 --> 00:17:07.114
Wataya.

00:17:07.114 --> 00:17:08.314
Yes.

00:17:08.314 --> 00:17:10.284
From what I've investigated,

00:17:10.284 --> 00:17:13.494
I have learned that someone
lured her there with a letter

00:17:13.494 --> 00:17:17.324
that told her to be there
at that specific time.

00:17:17.324 --> 00:17:20.494
In other words, her falling was neither
an accident nor a suicide attempt;

00:17:20.494 --> 00:17:23.434
it was someone's plan.

00:17:23.434 --> 00:17:26.704
So who pushed her off then?

00:17:26.704 --> 00:17:28.804
<i>Was it Narumi-kun there?</i>

00:17:28.804 --> 00:17:33.444
Unfortunately, no. She fell by herself.

00:17:33.444 --> 00:17:35.114
You say strange things.

00:17:35.114 --> 00:17:37.184
Yes, it was strange.

00:17:37.184 --> 00:17:42.054
But strange things always
have a hidden truth.

00:17:42.054 --> 00:17:44.454
This is the trick you set up,

00:17:44.454 --> 00:17:48.624
the unseen hands that you used
to push her off the landing.

00:17:48.624 --> 00:17:51.394
Hands? Aren't those sunglasses?

00:17:51.394 --> 00:17:54.064
He's saying that her glasses
are the main point.

00:17:54.064 --> 00:17:56.934
The victim was summoned
to the emergency stairs

00:17:56.934 --> 00:17:59.464
by a letter someone sent her.

00:17:59.464 --> 00:18:01.474
Even though she was
suspicious of the letter,

00:18:01.474 --> 00:18:03.974
she was attracted by what it said.

00:18:03.974 --> 00:18:06.974
She desperately wanted
to know about her past.

00:18:06.974 --> 00:18:09.744
So she went to the landing.

00:18:09.744 --> 00:18:12.744
But there was no one there.

00:18:12.744 --> 00:18:16.414
So she would have naturally
looked around the area.

00:18:16.414 --> 00:18:21.554
And then she noticed someone
looking up at her from the ground.

00:18:21.554 --> 00:18:23.294
Then, because she's near-sighted,

00:18:23.294 --> 00:18:27.294
she put her glasses on to
better see who it was...

00:18:27.294 --> 00:18:29.164
Now comes the key.

00:18:30.234 --> 00:18:33.164
What would happen if those glasses
had been switched with another pair

00:18:33.164 --> 00:18:35.764
that weren't the right prescription?

00:18:37.804 --> 00:18:40.044
After suddenly losing her balance,

00:18:40.044 --> 00:18:45.444
she tried to cling to the deadly fence
that had been worked on in advance.

00:18:45.444 --> 00:18:47.254
She realized only too late
that it had been modified

00:18:47.254 --> 00:18:50.524
to send her and the fence
crashing to the ground.

00:18:50.524 --> 00:18:56.194
However, the culprit was
unlucky in two different ways.

00:18:56.194 --> 00:18:59.264
First, on the day it happened, a
truck was parked beneath the landing

00:18:59.264 --> 00:19:05.134
in a spot where a different
car was usually parked.

00:19:05.134 --> 00:19:07.534
If that truck hadn't acted as a cushion,

00:19:07.534 --> 00:19:09.604
she would have unquestionably
died an instant death.

00:19:09.604 --> 00:19:14.274
Second, when the culprit
recovered the switched glasses and

00:19:14.274 --> 00:19:18.984
switched them again with
a pre-broken pair...

00:19:18.984 --> 00:19:22.344
...he unfortunately cut his fingers!

00:19:24.324 --> 00:19:27.094
The investigators even found shards of glass

00:19:27.094 --> 00:19:28.884
from a different prescription...

00:19:29.854 --> 00:19:34.134
The melody of logic always plays the truth.

00:19:34.134 --> 00:19:36.534
<i>Sonobe-sensei. The one who did this...</i>

00:19:41.704 --> 00:19:43.034
...was you!

00:19:43.604 --> 00:19:47.564
<i>Narumi-san's no ordinary person...</i>

00:19:49.644 --> 00:19:51.144
<i>Narumi-kun...</i>

00:19:51.144 --> 00:19:54.454
The culprit was unlucky in another way.

00:19:54.454 --> 00:19:59.254
He was unfortunate enough to cross you...

00:19:59.254 --> 00:20:03.464
...Kiyotaka Narumi's younger brother.

00:20:03.464 --> 00:20:06.164
<i>How do you know about Kiyotaka-san?!</i>

00:20:06.164 --> 00:20:11.264
Who are you? Why did you try
to kill Sayoko Shiranagatani?!

00:20:11.264 --> 00:20:13.234
The Blade Children...

00:20:14.474 --> 00:20:16.174
What?

00:20:16.174 --> 00:20:18.474
"I'm going to pursue the
mystery of the Blade Children..."

00:20:19.644 --> 00:20:21.804
The Blade Children...

00:20:25.284 --> 00:20:26.214
Sonobe!

00:20:26.214 --> 00:20:27.584
Stop!

00:20:43.034 --> 00:20:45.704
Over here, Assistant Inspector!

00:20:45.704 --> 00:20:47.494
Look!

00:20:49.034 --> 00:20:51.064
What the?!

00:20:54.074 --> 00:20:56.174
Why did Sonobe...

00:20:57.714 --> 00:21:04.644
<i>What exactly are the Blade Children?</i>

00:21:06.784 --> 00:21:12.484
<i>A sweet scent washes into my throat</i>

00:21:12.484 --> 00:21:19.184
<i>and my feelings continuously overflow...</i>

00:21:31.304 --> 00:21:37.344
<i>Don't look at me with that same gaze</i>

00:21:37.344 --> 00:21:42.984
<i>that's like you're following a soccer ball.</i>

00:21:42.984 --> 00:21:48.894
<i>I've already grown used to
my third year at the office,</i>

00:21:48.894 --> 00:21:55.464
<i>but did I lose something instead?</i>

00:21:55.464 --> 00:22:01.204
<i>Those days long ago when we
would talk about anything...</i>

00:22:01.204 --> 00:22:06.404
<i>We're finally old enough now</i>

00:22:06.404 --> 00:22:12.244
<i>to have those slightly awkward
discussions about love.</i>

00:22:12.244 --> 00:22:23.854
<i>A single day seems so long,
but a whole year ends so quickly.</i>

00:22:23.854 --> 00:22:29.634
<i>A whole year seems so short,</i>

00:22:29.634 --> 00:22:35.934
<i>but how well will I be able
to live the rest of my life?</i>

00:22:40.534 --> 00:22:43.804
Time for Hiyono's Useful News Report!

00:22:43.804 --> 00:22:45.404
What in the world's going on?

00:22:45.404 --> 00:22:47.534
There's suddenly a mountain
of mysteries lately!

00:22:47.534 --> 00:22:50.444
There's no taking your
eyes off the Spiral now!

00:22:50.444 --> 00:22:53.344
<i>Next episode's highlights include
Narumi-san's great kitchen knife skills</i>

00:22:53.344 --> 00:22:55.544
<i>and Hiyono-chan's information assault!</i>

00:22:55.544 --> 00:22:57.444
Who's the killer?!

00:22:57.444 --> 00:22:59.114
Just kidding!

00:22:59.114 --> 00:23:01.754
What happens next time is top secret!

00:23:01.754 --> 00:23:03.784
On the next Spiral: Bond of Reasoning...

00:23:03.784 --> 00:23:04.724
The Manor of Death

00:23:04.724 --> 00:23:06.024
Be sure to watch it, okay?

00:23:06.024 --> 00:23:08.754
That's all for today's Hiyono's Playhouse!
